v2.1
- New: wifi-watchdog service (SetupHelper-managed, always on). The BCM43455
  firmware can wedge hard in concurrent STA+AP use (raspberrypi/linux#7092,
  chanspec -52 storms, WiFi dead until power cycle - observed twice during
  validation, once triggered by a mere password change, i.e. the native
  svc -t restart, with a client connecting). The watchdog detects the wedge
  (fresh -52 errors with the station down, or a zombie AP, 3 consecutive
  30s checks), then recovers: stop AP -> reload brcmfmac -> reboot as last
  resort (rate-limited to one per 15 min). Forensics persist in
  /data/log/wifi-ap/ (/var/log is tmpfs and dies with the power cycle).

v2.0
- Rewrite: the AP no longer needs hostapd (absent from the arm64/raspberrypi5
  feeds). The engine files/wifi-ap-run runs the image's wpa_supplicant in AP
  mode (mode=2, CONFIG_AP) on a virtual ap0 created NEXT TO the wlan0 station:
  concurrent STA+AP, like a Cerbo GX. Validated on Pi 5 / BCM43455 / Venus 3.75
  with a real client (association, DHCP lease, NAT traffic), the wlan0 client
  connection staying up throughout.
- New: native UI integration. setup installs the hostapd service TEMPLATE
  (/opt/victronenergy/service-templates/hostapd/ + the empty marker
  conf/hostapd.conf that venus-platform's templateExists() checks). Once
  venus-platform restarts it publishes /Services/AccessPoint/Enabled: the
  stock "Create access point" toggle appears in Settings > Wi-Fi in BOTH GUIs
  and installs/removes /service/hostapd through svectl - exactly the Cerbo
  flow. No QML is patched.
- New: password via /Settings/Services/AccessPointPassword (declared with
  AddSettings; venus-platform natively restarts the service when it changes),
  with PASSWORD from wifi-ap.conf as fallback (8-63 chars enforced).
- New: channel follows the wlan0 station when it is associated (single-radio
  constraint); falls back to CHANNEL from wifi-ap.conf when the station is
  not connected (van use case) or sits on a DFS channel. Second start attempt
  on the fallback channel if the first frequency is refused.
- Change: NAT is now egress-agnostic (MASQUERADE scoped to the AP subnet,
  whatever the default route is: wwan0 in the van, wlan0/eth0 elsewhere).
  UPSTREAM in wifi-ap.conf is no longer used; old fixed-upstream rules are
  cleaned up on start and uninstall.
- Removed: the no-op services/wifi-ap placeholder (and its INSTALL_SERVICES).
  setup removes it from existing installs, along with legacy hostapd-native.
- Removed: the dummy /data/venus/serial-number hack. The engine does not
  derive the SSID from the serial, and venus-platform's gate is only the
  template marker.
- Uninstall: disables the AP, mirrors svectl -r if venus-platform is down,
  restores the stock template where one existed (Cerbo-like images) or
  removes ours, and tears down ap0/NAT/DHCP leftovers.

v1.2
- Fix: services/wifi-ap/run carried a UTF-8 BOM, so the kernel did not see a
  valid shebang and runsv could not exec it. Combined with "sleep infinity"
  (a GNU extension BusyBox sleep rejects), the no-op service was restarted
  once a second forever.
- Fix: removed services/wifi-ap/finish. It dated from v1, when this service
  owned the AP. Since v2 the AP belongs to /service/hostapd, but finish still
  deleted ap0, killed dnsmasq and removed the NAT rules on every stop of the
  no-op service - tearing down a live AP owned by another service. setup now
  deletes it from installs that already have it.
- Fix: clamp TCP MSS to the path MTU on the upstream interface. A cellular
  upstream is typically MTU 1450; without this, clients hit PMTU black holes
  where small requests work and larger responses never arrive.
- Improvement: MASQUERADE is now scoped to the AP subnet instead of every
  packet leaving the upstream interface. The old unscoped rule is deleted on
  start and on uninstall, so upgrading leaves no duplicate.
- Improvement: default DHCP lease raised from 2m to 12h. Existing
  wifi-ap.conf files are preserved and keep their current value.
- Cleanup: repaired mojibake in the hostapd template comments.

v1.1
- Fix: detect hostapd binary explicitly in service run script (/usr/sbin, /usr/bin, PATH)
- Fix: clear error message when hostapd is missing, with install hint
- Fix: cleanup FORWARD iptables rules on ap0 (not wlan0) in finish script
- Fix: stop dnsmasq-ap0 and remove ap0 virtual interface during service stop
- Improvement: setup now attempts to auto-install hostapd via opkg when missing

v1.0
- Initial release
- WiFi AP on ap0 virtual interface (BCM43438 / RPi3)
- Custom SSID + WPA2-PSK via wifi-ap.conf
- dnsmasq DHCP for clients (192.168.0.100-200)
- iptables NAT: ap0 -> wwan0 (4G internet sharing)
- Disables connman tethering (conflict with ap0)
- Compatible SetupHelper (install/uninstall/reinstall)
